3.2 Scrolling
=============

Option                            Default           Meaning
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘subtle-scroll-style’             paged             ‘paged’ keeps text still until the page turns; ‘continuous’ keeps the spoken line at ‘subtle-focus-ratio’.
‘subtle-focus-ratio’              2/3               Where the spoken line sits (0.5 is the middle).
‘subtle-page-margin’              2                 Free lines below the spoken line before the page turns.
‘subtle-page-top-margin’          0                 Free lines above it.  Kept below ‘subtle-page-lead’.
‘subtle-page-lead’                1                 Lines above the spoken line after a page turn.
‘subtle-hold-pause-lines’         nil               Pause playback while a held word is this many lines above the spoken one.
‘subtle-move-point’               unless-selected   Whether autoscroll moves the cursor: ‘always’, ‘never’ or ‘unless-selected’.
‘subtle-move-idle-cursor’         t                 An idle cursor keeps following the cue.
‘subtle-resume-delay’             5                 Seconds before autoscroll resumes.
‘subtle-auto-resume’              t                 Resume by itself.
‘subtle-scroll-commands’          list              Commands that count as scrolling by hand.
‘subtle-popup-style’              box               The notice: ‘box’, ‘echo-area’ or ‘none’.
‘subtle-warn-continuous-scroll’   t                 Warn when ‘continuous’ is used with bltzread.


