3.3 Text
========

Option                           Default            Meaning
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘subtle-layout’                  single-spaced      See Layouts above.
‘subtle-paragraph-source’        explicit-and-gap   ‘explicit’ or ‘explicit-and-gap’.
‘subtle-paragraph-gap’           1.0                Silence after a sentence that ends a paragraph.
‘subtle-paragraph-pause’         1.75               Seconds paused at a break in ‘paragraph-pause’.
‘subtle-sentence-terminators’    ".?!…。！？؟"      Characters that end a sentence.
‘subtle-sentence-closers’        regexp             Characters allowed after a terminator.
‘subtle-cue-fill-column’         nil                Wrap long cues at this width (non-paragraph layouts).
‘subtle-paragraph-fill-column’   nil                Fill paragraphs to this width.
‘subtle-text-scale’              1.3                Size of the text (1.0 is normal).
‘subtle-use-variable-pitch’      t                  Use the ‘variable-pitch’ face.
‘subtle-language-codes’          alist              Maps the language part of ‘movie.sl.srt’ to your code (sl gives "slv"); an unlisted two or three letter part is used as it is.
‘subtle-control-strip’           see below          Commands shown in the strip at the top.

   The strip is an alist of (COMMAND .  LABEL). The key shown is looked
up in ‘subtle-mode-map’, so rebinding a key changes the strip too:

     (setopt subtle-control-strip
             '((subtle-toggle-pause . "pause")
               (subtle-previous-cue . "prev")
               (subtle-next-cue . "next")
               (subtle-help . "help")))


