3.4 Blitz reading
=================

Blitz reading makes point follow the playback: at every new cue it jumps
to the word a package chose (bltzread: the first unknown one), or to the
start of the cue when none was chosen.  \m switches it on and off.
Moving point off the cue pauses it until point is back on the cue.
Moving point less than ‘subtle-blitz-nav-grace’ seconds before a cue
change releases it as well, so a word you are just reading is not
snatched away.  A card that is open when point moves is dismissed, and
‘subtle-blitz-moved-functions’ then lets a package show something for
the new word: bltzread opens its card there, so no key is needed.

Option                     Default   Meaning
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘subtle-blitz-follow’      t         Point jumps to the chosen word of each new cue.
‘subtle-blitz-nav-grace’   0.25      Moving point this many seconds before a cue change releases blitz.
‘subtle-blitz-indicator’   t         Show a small corner box while blitz is on.


File: subtle.info,  Node: Popups,  Prev: Blitz reading,  Up: Options

3.5 Popups
==========

Option                            Default   Meaning
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘subtle-popup-box-style’          unicode   Box drawing characters: ‘unicode’ or ‘ascii’.
‘subtle-popup-frame-parameters’   nil       Frame parameters merged over the defaults of the child frames; yours win.

     (setopt subtle-popup-box-style 'ascii
             subtle-popup-frame-parameters '((internal-border-width . 4)))


